IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g3-nouns`
IMPORT `g3-art10-public-access`
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art19-reportable-matters`
IMPORT `g6-art20-court-orders`
IMPORT `g7-interpretation`
IMPORT `g7-art21-23-expressions`
IMPORT `g7-art37-43-final`
IMPORT `g8-nouns`
IMPORT `g8-art26-demand`
IMPORT `g8-art29-31-information`
IMPORT `g8-penalties`
IMPORT `g9-interpretation`
IMPORT `g9-common`
IMPORT `g9-sched2-tribunal`
IMPORT `int-readings`
IMPORT `int-nouns`
IMPORT `int-commencement`
IMPORT `int-vintage`
IMPORT `int-wiring`

-- int-h-offence.l4: headline (d) of the integration layer: what offence, and what penalty, for this act?
-- Six offences carry a penalty as data in the groups that own them -- Article 19(10) and (11) (group G6: 12 months and a fine), Article 20(6) (G6: 24 months and a fine), Articles 21 and 23 (G7: strict, level 3;
-- knowing, 24 months and a fine), Article 26(7) (G8: 3 months and level 3), 26(10) and 29(1) (G8: 24 months and a fine). Article 37(1) (G7) makes an officer of a partnership or a body corporate guilty of the
-- body's offence when it was committed with the officer's consent or connivance, with "the penalty provided for that offence" (IP30), and Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f) (G9) caps the penalty that Regulations
-- may attach to an offence in relation to the Charity Tribunal at imprisonment for 2 years and a fine. This module joins the owner of the penalty (IP30) to Article 37 and to the cap.
-- The amount of a fine is not in the sources: "level 3 on the standard scale" has no money amount and "a fine" has no maximum, so a penalty here is the term of imprisonment in months and the KIND of fine.
-- It rests on the Articles that create the offence, Article 37 and Schedule 2, and refuses for a day before they were in force and for a day on which the text changed and the two texts answer differently.

§ `Integration layer -- headline (d): the offence and the penalty for an act`

-- generated by gen_replace.py: a copy of `Facts for Article 37` (module g7-art37-43-final) with the field `the body committed an offence under this Law` replaced
GIVEN original IS A `Facts for Article 37` @desc The record to copy
      replacement IS A BOOLEAN @desc The new value of the field `the body committed an offence under this Law`
GIVETH A `Facts for Article 37`
`Int the facts for Article 37 with the offence` original replacement MEANS
    `Facts for Article 37` WITH
        `kind of body` IS original's `kind of body`
        `the body committed an offence under this Law` IS replacement
        `consent or connivance is proved` IS original's `consent or connivance is proved`
        `capacity` IS original's `capacity`
        `how the person comes within the capacity` IS original's `how the person comes within the capacity`


-- The act alleged.
DECLARE `Act alleged in the case` IS ONE OF
    `a statement about an entity`
        HAS body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The entity the statement is about; the kinds of entity and the Jersey-entity status are derived by group G1
            `facts for the excepted foreign charity test` IS A `Facts for the excepted foreign charity test` @desc Group G7's facts for Article 22
            `the entity is wholly or mainly managed or controlled in or from within Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 23(3)(c)
            statement IS A `Statement about an entity under Articles 21 to 23` @desc The statement, its context, who is aware of what and who intends what
    `acting as a governor after reporting a reportable matter`
        HAS `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity is a registered charity (Article 19(10))
            position IS A `Position of a governor under Article 19(2)` @desc When the matter arose and was reported
            permissions IS A LIST OF `Permission to act as a governor` @desc The permissions given to the person
            `the act is done in accordance with any condition on the permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act is within any condition on the permission
            `the person has a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Article 19(11): a reasonable excuse
    `contravening a disqualification order`
        HAS contravenes IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person contravenes the disqualification order (Article 20(6))
    `failing to comply with a requirement under Article 26`
        HAS facts IS A `Facts of a contravention under Article 26(7)` @desc The facts of the contravention
    `giving false information under Article 26`
        HAS facts IS A `Facts of providing information under Article 26(10)` @desc What the person provided, knew and intended
    `disclosing restricted information under Article 29`
        HAS body IS A `Body in the case` @desc The entity whose register entry the information may be (Article 10(3), group G3: IP25 is decided from it)
            matter IS A `Matter entered on the register` @desc The matter on the register that the information is (Article 10(3))
            `the Commissioner has designated the matter as not a public part of the register` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has designated the matter as not public (Article 10(5))
            info IS AN `Information received and its character` @desc What the information is and how it was received
            disclosure IS A `Disclosure of information` @desc The disclosure

DECLARE `Offence case` HAS
    act IS AN `Act alleged in the case` @desc The act alleged to be an offence
    officer IS A MAYBE `Facts for Article 37` @desc The officer of a body whose consent or connivance is alleged (Article 37(1)); NOTHING if no officer is in question

DECLARE `Offence and penalty` HAS
    `an offence is made out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act is an offence under the Law
    penalties IS A LIST OF `Penalty provided` @desc The penalty or penalties the act carries (IP30): one per offence made out (an act can make out two offences: Articles 21(1) and 21(2))
    `the officer is also guilty under Article 37(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Group G7: Article 37(1): the officer consented to or connived at an offence of a partnership or body corporate
    `the penalties of the officer` IS A LIST OF `Penalty provided` @desc Group G7: Article 37(1): the penalty provided for the offence, carried to the officer
    `every penalty is within the cap of Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Group G9: Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f): whether every penalty is within imprisonment for 2 years and a fine

-- The penalties of the act, and whether an offence is made out.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law
      act IS AN `Act alleged in the case` @desc The act
GIVETH A LIST OF `Penalty provided`
`Int (d) the penalties of the act` readings day vintage act MEANS
    CONSIDER act
      WHEN `a statement about an entity` body exceptedFacts managed statement THEN
            `Art 21 and 23: the penalties for the statement` entity registered excepted managed statement (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
            WHERE
                notices MEANS EMPTY
                entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day body
                registered MEANS `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity
                excepted MEANS `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` exceptedFacts registered
      WHEN `acting as a governor after reporting a reportable matter` registered position permissions accordance excuse THEN
            IF `Art 19(11) the person commits an offence` (`Art 19(10) the person contravenes paragraph (10)` (readings's `reading of Articles 15 to 20`) registered position permissions day accordance) excuse
            THEN LIST `Art 19(11) the penalty for contravening Article 19(10)`
            ELSE EMPTY
      WHEN `contravening a disqualification order` contravenes THEN
            IF `Art 20(6) the person commits an offence` contravenes THEN LIST `Art 20(6) the penalty for contravening a disqualification order` ELSE EMPTY
      WHEN `failing to comply with a requirement under Article 26` facts THEN
            maybeToList (`Art 26(7) the penalty the person is liable to` facts)
      WHEN `giving false information under Article 26` facts THEN
            maybeToList (`Art 26(10) the penalty the person is liable to` facts)
      WHEN `disclosing restricted information under Article 29` body matter designated info disclosure THEN
            maybeToList (`Art 29(1) the penalty the person is liable to` (readings's `reading of Articles 26 to 36`) (`Art 10(3) the matter is in a public part of the register` (readings's `reading of Articles 8 to 10`) entity matter designated) info disclosure)
            WHERE
                notices MEANS EMPTY
                entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day body

-- Whether a contravention of Article 21 or 23 is the BODY's own offence: paragraphs (1), (3), (5) of Article 21 and (1) of Article 23 bind the entity alone; paragraphs (2), (4), (6) of Article 21 and (2) of
-- Article 23 bind "an entity or other person", and are the entity's when the entity itself made the statement (Article 21(7), 23(5)).
GIVEN c IS A `Contravention of Article 21 or Article 23` @desc The contravention
      `made by the entity itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the statement was made by the entity itself
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Int the contravention is an offence of the body` c `made by the entity itself` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
      WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 21` THEN TRUE
      WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 21` THEN `made by the entity itself`
      WHEN `paragraph (3) of Article 21` THEN TRUE
      WHEN `paragraph (4) of Article 21` THEN `made by the entity itself`
      WHEN `paragraph (5) of Article 21` THEN TRUE
      WHEN `paragraph (6) of Article 21` THEN `made by the entity itself`
      WHEN `paragraph (1) of Article 23` THEN TRUE
      WHEN `paragraph (2) of Article 23` THEN `made by the entity itself`

-- The penalties of the offences the BODY committed, which Article 37(1) carries to an officer who consented or connived. For an act other than a statement, the act's penalties.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law
      act IS AN `Act alleged in the case` @desc The act
GIVETH A LIST OF `Penalty provided`
`Int (d) the penalties of the body's own offences` readings day vintage act MEANS
    CONSIDER act
      WHEN `a statement about an entity` body exceptedFacts managed statement THEN
            map (GIVEN c YIELD `Art 21 and 23 the penalty for the contravention` c)
                (filter (GIVEN c YIELD `Int the contravention is an offence of the body` c (`the person making the statement is the entity` statement))
                    (`Art 21 and 23: the contraventions made out by the statement` entity registered excepted managed statement (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)))
            WHERE
                notices MEANS EMPTY
                entity MEANS `Int IP5 the entity` readings vintage notices day body
                registered MEANS `Int IP6 the entity is a registered charity` entity
                excepted MEANS `Art 22 the entity is an excepted foreign charity` exceptedFacts registered
      WHEN `acting as a governor after reporting a reportable matter` registered position permissions accordance excuse THEN `Int (d) the penalties of the act` readings day vintage act
      WHEN `contravening a disqualification order` contravenes THEN `Int (d) the penalties of the act` readings day vintage act
      WHEN `failing to comply with a requirement under Article 26` facts THEN `Int (d) the penalties of the act` readings day vintage act
      WHEN `giving false information under Article 26` facts THEN `Int (d) the penalties of the act` readings day vintage act
      WHEN `disclosing restricted information under Article 29` body matter designated info disclosure THEN `Int (d) the penalties of the act` readings day vintage act

-- The units the question rests on, by the offence.
GIVEN act IS AN `Act alleged in the case` @desc The act
GIVETH A LIST OF `Unit of the Law`
`Int (d) the units the question rests on` act MEANS
    CONSIDER act
      WHEN `a statement about an entity` body excepted managed statement THEN LIST `Int Article` 21, `Int Article` 22, `Int Article` 23, `Int Article` 37, `Int Schedule` 2
      WHEN `acting as a governor after reporting a reportable matter` registered position permissions accordance excuse THEN LIST `Int Article` 19, `Int Article` 37, `Int Schedule` 2
      WHEN `contravening a disqualification order` contravenes THEN LIST `Int Article` 20, `Int Article` 37, `Int Schedule` 2
      WHEN `failing to comply with a requirement under Article 26` facts THEN LIST `Int Article` 26, `Int Article` 37, `Int Schedule` 2
      WHEN `giving false information under Article 26` facts THEN LIST `Int Article` 26, `Int Article` 37, `Int Schedule` 2
      WHEN `disclosing restricted information under Article 29` body matter designated info disclosure THEN LIST `Int Article` 29, `Int Article` 10, `Int Article` 37, `Int Schedule` 2

-- The answer under ONE text of the Law.
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The readings of the fleet
      day IS A DATE @desc The day asked about
      vintage IS A `Vintage of the text` @desc The text of the Law
      case IS AN `Offence case` @desc The case
GIVETH AN `Offence and penalty`
`Int (d) the offence and the penalty under the text` readings day vintage case MEANS
    `Offence and penalty` WITH
        `an offence is made out` IS NOT null thePenalties
        penalties IS thePenalties
        `the officer is also guilty under Article 37(1)` IS
            CONSIDER case's officer
              WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
              WHEN JUST facts THEN `Art 37(1) the person is also guilty of the offence` (`Int the facts for Article 37 with the offence` facts (NOT null bodyPenalties)) g7
        `the penalties of the officer` IS
            CONSIDER case's officer
              WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
              WHEN JUST facts THEN concat (map (GIVEN p YIELD maybeToList (`Art 37(1) the penalty of the person who is also guilty` (`Int the facts for Article 37 with the offence` facts (NOT null bodyPenalties)) p g7)) bodyPenalties)
        `every penalty is within the cap of Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f)` IS all (GIVEN p YIELD `Sch 2 para 4(3)(f) the penalty is within the cap` (readings's `reading of Schedules 1 and 2`) p day) thePenalties
    WHERE
        g7 MEANS readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`
        thePenalties MEANS `Int (d) the penalties of the act` readings day vintage (case's act)
        bodyPenalties MEANS `Int (d) the penalties of the body's own offences` readings day vintage (case's act)

@export What offence, and what penalty, an act carries under the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014: a statement about an entity (Articles 21 and 23: strict offences with a fine of level 3, knowing offences with 24 months and a fine), acting as a governor after reporting a reportable matter (Article 19(10) and (11)), contravening a disqualification order (Article 20(6)), failing to comply with a demand for information (Article 26(7)), giving false information (Article 26(10)) and disclosing restricted information (Article 29(1)); whether the officer of a partnership or body corporate is also guilty and with what penalty (Article 37(1)); and whether every penalty is within the cap of Schedule 2 paragraph 4(3)(f). Refuses for a day before the Articles that create the offence were in force (Part 6: 1 January 2019), and for a day on which the text changed and the two texts answer differently
GIVEN readings IS A `Readings of the fleet` @desc The reading taken at each fork of the nine groups (the favoured readings are `Int the favoured readings of the fleet`)
      day IS A DATE @desc The day on which the act is done and the question asked, for example 2026-10-02 (ISO 8601)
      case IS AN `Offence case` @desc The act alleged and, if an officer of a body is in question, the facts Article 37(1) reads
GIVETH AN `Offence and penalty`
`Int (d) the offence and the penalty for the act` readings day case MEANS
    `Int the answer if every unit is in force` (`Int (d) the units the question rests on` (case's act)) day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
        (`Int the answer under every text of the Law in force on` day (readings's `reading of Articles 21 to 25, 37 to 43 and the endnotes`)
            (GIVEN vintage YIELD `Int (d) the offence and the penalty under the text` readings day vintage case))
